      "writtenOn": "2026-05-29T18:33:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I believe that Matt\u0027s previous version stores the hash of the ensured cipd_manifest.txt in the separate stamp file, and compares the hash with the hash of the latest cipd_manifest.txt to validate the cache, right?\n\nI prefer the content-based approach over  mtime  because the timestamp approach carries assumptions about how Git and CIPD manage the timestamp of the manifest file.\n\nFor instance, Git checkouts to a specific revision on a CI bot could trigger false-positive runs, which are hard to debug. Unless there are meaningful benefits to  mtime  other than saving 15ms, I\u0027d prefer to go with the content-based approach as it is more robust.",
      "parentUuid": "5fce02ed_2d7e91dd",
